# --- Fuime -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe mode. Defaults to "test" everywhere, including production, until the
# money-transmission structure is legally settled (PRODUCTION_READINESS.md §1.5).
STRIPE_MODE="test"

# Signing secret for POST /fuime/webhooks/stripe (from `stripe listen`).
# Without it, webhooks are rejected rather than trusted unverified.
FUIME_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Where uploaded receipts go. MUST be "amazon" in any deployed environment —
# "local" is an ephemeral container disk and loses every receipt on deploy.
ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE="local"
S3__BUCKET=""
S3__REGION=""
S3__ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
S3__SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""

# Inbound domain for receipt-by-email. Leave blank to hide the feature; do NOT
# point it at hcb.hackclub.com.
FUIME_RECEIPT_PARSE_DOMAIN=""

# Comma-separated emails for admin/ops alerts (was hardcoded Hack Club staff).
FUIME_ENGINEER_EMAILS=""

# The Fuime agreement, signed at application time. Leave the template id blank
# and the whole signing step is skipped: applications are approved with nothing
# signed. Set all three to turn signing on. Roles and field names in the
# DocuSeal template must match exactly — see docs/fuime/DOCUSEAL_SETUP.md.
# Must be Fuime's own DocuSeal account, never Hack Club's templates.
FUIME_DOCUSEAL_TEMPLATE_ID=""
DOCUSEAL=""
DOCUSEAL__WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# The marketing site's waitlist, read-only, for /admin/waitlist. The SITE
# (site/api/waitlist.js on the fuime-site service) writes these keys; Rails only
# issues SCARD/SMEMBERS/HGETALL, and the rake backfill is the one writer.
#
# Set it EXPLICITLY — there is deliberately no fallback to REDIS_URL. Falling
# back would mean a service that simply forgot this variable reads the Sidekiq
# instance, finds no roster, and reports an empty waitlist instead of a missing
# one. Blank here is fine and honest: the page says it has nothing to read.
# Locally, point it at your dev Redis on a database of its own.
WAITLIST_REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379/2"

# The waitlist target on the admin progress bar. Defaults to 1000.
WAITLIST_GOAL=""

# --- Structural flags ---------------------------------------------------------
# These change what Fuime legally IS, so they are deliberately env vars rather
# than Flipper flags: a Flipper flag is a checkbox any admin can tick, and the
# failure mode here is a felony rather than a bad rollout. See
# app/lib/fuime/features.rb.
#
# Does Fuime hold customer funds, via a sponsor bank partner?
#
# OFF, and off is the shipping posture. It gates stored balances presented as
# spendable, card issuing, ACH/wire/check origination, and balance fronting —
# every path that implies money sits in an account Fuime controls on a user's
# behalf. Fuime has no banking licence, so with this off Fuime is not a
# custodian: money reaching Fuime's Stripe balance is Fuime's own revenue from
# its own sale, and what an operator is owed is a PAYABLE, not a deposit.
#
# Only the word "true" (any case) turns it on. "1", "yes" and "on" do not.
# Turning it on ALSO requires FUIME_SPONSOR_BANK_PARTNER, or the app refuses to
# boot in production/staging (config/initializers/fuime_safety_check.rb) —
# somebody has to name the institution actually holding the money.
FEATURE_SPONSOR_BANKING=""

# The institution holding customer funds. Required when the flag above is on,
# ignored otherwise. Not a credential — a name, so that "who has the money?" has
# a written answer before anyone can serve traffic that assumes one.
FUIME_SPONSOR_BANK_PARTNER=""
